# Netcheck report: {{ e.env }}

Generated by `playbooks/netcheck.yml`. Requirements: `docs/network-requirements.md`.
Probe = container on the jump box with one macvlan leg (own MAC) per test port group.

## N4/N9 Planned addresses are free (must not answer)
{% set answered = (jb.nc_free.results | default([])) | selectattr('rc', 'defined') | selectattr('rc', 'equalto', 0) | map(attribute='item') | list %}
- {{ res(answered | length == 0) }}: {{ (jb.nc_free.results | default([])) | length }} addresses checked{% if answered %}; **answering: {{ answered | join(', ') }}**{% endif %}

## N1/N4/N5/N6 Reachability per network and MTU (DF ping)
"jump box" = the probe's macvlan leg on relaxed port groups, the jump box's own address on the others
({{ nc_own_nets | default([]) | join(', ') or 'none' }}).

| Host | Network | MTU | host → jump box | jump box → host |
|---|---|---|---|---|
{% for h in hosts %}
{%   for p in hostvars[h].nc_host.ping | default([]) %}
{%     set net, mtu = p[0][0], p[0][1] %}
{%     set back = ((jb.nc_probe_ping.results | default([])) + (jb.nc_jb_ping.results | default([])))
              | selectattr('item', 'defined') | selectattr('rc', 'defined')
              | selectattr('item', 'equalto', [h, net, mtu]) | map(attribute='rc') | first | default('n/a') %}
| {{ h }} | {{ net }} | {{ mtu }} | {{ res(p[1] == 0) }} | {{ 'n/a' if back == 'n/a' else res(back == 0) }} |
{%   endfor %}
{% endfor %}

A 1500 failure is a layout problem. A 9000 failure only records that jumbo frames are not available end to end
(check the trunk NIC MTU below, the vSwitch MTU and the switches).

